m:out-out-critical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , re:Determination ;
    re:outputTier 0 ;
    re:outputConfidence 0 ;
    re:prescribesAction re:UrgentIntervention ;
    re:actionNarrative "Notify attending physician immediately. Order comprehensive cognitive evaluation (neuropsychological testing, imaging if not recent). Review and revise care plan within 48 hours. Assess for reversible causes: UTI, dehydration, medication side effects, depression-related pseudodementia. Increase supervision level. Notify family and document in medical record. Consult social work for advanced care planning discussion." .

m:seq-wellness-level3-good-age-adjusted
    a owl:NamedIndividual , re:CriticalEventSequence ;
    re:sequenceId "wellness-level3-good-age-adjusted" ;
    rdfs:label "Good Wellness — Age-Adjusted (Exercise Norm Calibrated, Five Dimensions In Norm)" ;
    rdfs:comment "For residents where the exercise norm has been age-adjusted (D7_AGE_ADJUSTED=H) — typically 75+ where standard exercise guidelines cannot be safely met — five non-exercise dimensions confirmed in norm is classified as GOOD rather than penalizing the resident against an inapplicable standard. Applies when D5_EXERCISE_OK=L is expected and acceptable given the resident's functional capacity." ;
